    private static string Explain(CommandDefinition c) => c.Id switch
    {
        CommandIds.LibraryFiles => "Show All Files in the Library to browse the workspace folder tree, expand folders and open documents.",
        CommandIds.LibraryRecent => "Show Recent workspaces, saved files and URLs in the Library. Click a workspace to restore its saved working context; Remove from Recent forgets only the reference.",
        CommandIds.LibrarySearch => "Show the latest workspace Search results in the Library. Run Search in Workspace to enter a new text query.",
        CommandIds.LibraryBacklinks => "Show workspace documents that link to the active saved document. Select a result to inspect the referring source.",
        CommandIds.LibraryBrokenLinks => "Show unresolved workspace links in the Library. Select a result to inspect its source and intended target before repair.",
        CommandIds.LibraryTasks => "Scan and show task-list items from workspace documents. Select a task to navigate to its source line.",
        CommandIds.Help => "Search feature names, meanings and prerequisites. Choose a beginner tutorial, move Back or Next, replay it, or exit at any time. Tutorials never edit documents automatically.",
        CommandIds.AIConnections => "Open Edit → Settings → AI connections → Manage AI connections. Follow Choose service, Configure connection, then Validate and save. Validate sends a fixed test message using the selected model; errors explain what to correct. Save stores settings and protects keys in Windows Credential Manager. The AI service menu includes GitHub Copilot and MCP server alongside APIs. Create, modify, delete and validate saved connections here. All appear in the main toolbar: API and Copilot offer Write with AI; MCP offers Open MCP tools. Website subscriptions do not imply API access.",
        CommandIds.AskAI => "Open Write with AI for the active note. Describe the change, check the scope and connection, then choose Generate for review. Compare the suggestion and choose Apply to use all proposed changes. Close or press Escape to discard. Applied edits are undoable.",
        CommandIds.AskKnowledge => "Ask a question in everyday language and get a short AI answer from your own notes, with the notes it used. Choose Edit → Explore your notes. Type a question naturally or choose a suggestion, replace any [bracket] word and press Find my notes. AI interprets the question; a search with no matches does not mean every note was read. Keep the notes that fit and press Get my answer. AI reads all the notes you keep ticked, in parts when needed, up to 1,000,000 characters per question. It names anything not read. A simple one-fact question may start with the best sections, then read the full ticked text if needed. Each part uses the selected connection's saved Characters to send at one time value. Version-range questions cover the full range. Then choose one: Copy for email, Save as PDF, Add to my note or Print. Tern prepares and checks one complete report before it is ready to share. Choose Use this checked report, then Preview report to read the formatted report. Review it once and tick I reviewed this report. Its executive summary comes first, followed by detailed findings, exact source evidence and a final review record. Copy for email builds a summary from that checked report on this computer; PDF, note and print keep the full report. Choosing another format reuses the same checked result instead of asking AI again. Editing the report or changing its sources requires a new check. Closing keeps unfinished work without contacting AI. Done finishes the task; Ask a new question starts again. Tern uses the AI selected in the top AI menu. If none exists, AI Connections opens first.",
        CommandIds.ReadCurrentLine => "Request a polite announcement of the source caret's line, column and text, without moving focus or changing the note. Very long lines are explicitly shortened to 2,000 characters for this announcement. Screen-reader behavior requires native acceptance.",
        CommandIds.ReadDocumentStatus => "Request a polite announcement of the active note's name, saved/unsaved state, source line and last analyzed word count. A pending count is identified as updating. No document text is copied into Activity or diagnostics.",
        CommandIds.Reset => "Select recent history, preferences, session restore state, search indexes or cached online documents/assets. Close all workspaces before clearing indexes, and close cached online tabs before clearing their cache. Open drafts, physical files, attachments, recovery copies and separately managed AI credentials are preserved.",
        CommandIds.ClearRecent => "Confirm removal of unpinned file, workspace and URL history and the Reopen Closed Tab list. Pins, open tabs and physical documents are kept. Reset Tern offers an explicit option to include pins.",
        CommandIds.MoveDocument => "Move the saved document to another folder in its workspace. Choose File → Document actions → Move Document…, or right-click it in the Library and choose Move to…, or drag it onto a folder. Tern never overwrites: an existing name in the destination is refused. Open tabs, version history, recent entries, recovery copies and linked-image permissions follow the file, and a link-review dialog proposes relative-link repairs.",
        CommandIds.DuplicateDocument => "Create a copy named \"name copy.ext\" beside the saved document and open nothing automatically. The copy is a new document: it starts with no version history, but inherits linked-image permissions and view settings. Also available from the Library context menu.",
        CommandIds.Rename => "Name a new local draft without creating a file, or rename a saved local file within its current folder. Right-click the tab and choose Rename, or use File → Rename Document…. Online copies must be downloaded first. Invalid names and collisions are refused. Review unsaved changes and save explicitly.",
