        CommandIds.InsertImage or CommandIds.PasteImage => "Save the note first. Insert Local Image first uses copied PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP or BMP files from the clipboard. If no copied image file is available, it opens the file picker. For Paste Image as Attachment, copy an image file in File Explorer or copy image pixels, then choose Format → Paste Image as Attachment. Ordinary Ctrl+V in the writing pane can also paste clipboard text; the explicit attachment command needs image data. An image file beside the Markdown file is linked immediately through drag-and-drop, Insert Local Image, Ctrl+V or Paste Image as Attachment. Images from other folders offer Link original or Copy image. Link uses the source path, including subfolders or other locations. Copy asks for a destination and links the new file. Paste Image as Attachment follows the same file rules. Only clipboard pixels without a source file go directly to the copy picker; if the file already exists, Tern asks first. Replace sends the old image to the Recycle Bin; Cancel keeps it. Check the preview and save the Markdown. Undo removes the link while the copied picture stays on disk.",
